    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Markets</span> are the mechanisms through which buyers and sellers come together to exchange goods, services, and information. Markets perform vital economic and social functions that facilitate trade, allocate resources, and connect producers with consumers.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. What is a Market?</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A market is any arrangement (physical, virtual, or institutional) that brings together buyers and sellers to facilitate exchange of goods, services, or resources. Examples: Mile 12 Market (physical), Amazon/Jumia (virtual/online), stock market (institutional).</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Functions/Roles of Markets</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Price determination</td><td>Supply and demand interact to set prices — markets discover what products are worth</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Facilitating exchange</td><td>Enable buyers and sellers to complete transactions efficiently</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Resource allocation</td><td>Distribute goods, services, and resources to where they are most valued</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Information dissemination</td><td>Price signals communicate information about scarcity, value, and opportunities</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Creating utility</td><td>Add value through form (processing), place (distribution), time (storage), possession (transfer of ownership)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Promoting specialisation</td><td>Markets allow producers to specialise in what they do best and trade for other needs</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Economic development</td><td>Facilitate trade and wealth creation that drive economic growth</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Types of Utility Created by Marketing</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Form utility:</strong> Transforming raw materials into products customers want (e.g., turning cocoa into chocolate)</li>\n  <li><strong>Place utility:</strong> Making products available where customers need them (e.g., delivering goods to Lagos from Kano)</li>\n  <li><strong>Time utility:</strong> Making products available when customers need them (e.g., storing rice harvested in July for sale in December)</li>\n  <li><strong>Possession utility:</strong> Transferring ownership from seller to buyer through exchange</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Types of Markets</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Consumer market</td><td>Individuals buy for personal use</td><td>Supermarket, fashion store</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Business/Industrial market</td><td>Organisations buy for production or operations</td><td>Raw material market</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Reseller market</td><td>Organisations buy to resell at profit</td><td>Wholesalers, retailers</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Government market</td><td>Government buys for public services</td><td>Military procurement</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>International market</td><td>Cross-border buyers and sellers</td><td>ECOWAS trade, global exports</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Markets create FOUR types of utility: Form, Place, Time, and Possession. A key function of markets is PRICE DETERMINATION through supply and demand. Remember: markets also include virtual markets (online shopping, stock exchange) — not just physical locations.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Markets bring buyers and sellers together to exchange. Functions: price determination, facilitate exchange, allocate resources, disseminate information, create utility (Form, Place, Time, Possession), promote specialisation, drive economic development. Types: consumer, business/industrial, reseller, government, international.\n</div>\n  ",
