    "topic": "Marketing Plan",
    "topicCode": "SS1-MKT-11",
    "module": "Marketing Strategy",
    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  A <span class=\"learn-keyword\">marketing plan</span> is a comprehensive document that outlines a business's marketing objectives, strategies, and tactics for a specific period. It serves as the roadmap for all marketing activities — ensuring they are coordinated, focused, and aligned with business goals.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of a Marketing Plan</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A marketing plan is a written document that outlines the marketing objectives of a business, the strategies and tactics to achieve those objectives, the budget required, and the methods for monitoring and evaluating performance over a specified time period (usually one year).</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Components/Sections of a Marketing Plan</h3>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Executive Summary:</strong> Brief overview of the entire plan's key points</li>\n  <li><strong>Situational Analysis:</strong> Where are we now? SWOT analysis; market analysis; competitor analysis</li>\n  <li><strong>Marketing Objectives:</strong> Where do we want to go? Specific, measurable, achievable goals (SMART)</li>\n  <li><strong>Target Market:</strong> Who are we targeting? Market segmentation and selection</li>\n  <li><strong>Marketing Strategies:</strong> How will we get there? Positioning, 4Ps strategies</li>\n  <li><strong>Marketing Tactics/Action Plans:</strong> Specific activities, timelines, and responsibilities</li>\n  <li><strong>Budget:</strong> Financial resources allocated to each marketing activity</li>\n  <li><strong>Implementation:</strong> Who does what, when, and how</li>\n  <li><strong>Monitoring and Evaluation:</strong> How will we measure success? KPIs, feedback mechanisms</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Importance of a Marketing Plan</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Provides direction and focus for all marketing activities</li>\n  <li>Ensures coordination across the organisation</li>\n  <li>Allocates resources efficiently</li>\n  <li>Provides a basis for monitoring and controlling marketing activities</li>\n  <li>Reduces risk by thorough pre-planning</li>\n  <li>Communicates strategy to all stakeholders</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Marketing objectives must be SMART: Specific (clear), Measurable (quantifiable), Achievable (realistic), Relevant (aligned with business goals), Time-bound (with a deadline). The situational analysis (SWOT) is the foundation of the marketing plan — you must know where you are before planning where to go.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Marketing plan = written roadmap for marketing activities. Components: executive summary, situational analysis (SWOT), objectives (SMART), target market, strategies (4Ps), tactics/action plans, budget, implementation, monitoring/evaluation. Importance: direction, coordination, resource allocation, control, risk reduction. Objectives must be SMART.\n</div>\n  ",
