    "topic": "Pricing Strategies and Determinants",
    "topicCode": "SS1-MKT-14",
    "module": "Pricing",
    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Pricing</span> is one of the most critical marketing decisions. Price is the amount of money customers must give up to obtain a product. It is the only element of the marketing mix that generates revenue, directly affects profitability, and signals product quality to customers.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Pricing Objectives</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Profit maximisation:</strong> Set prices to generate maximum profit</li>\n  <li><strong>Market share growth:</strong> Lower prices to attract more customers and grow market share</li>\n  <li><strong>Survival:</strong> Set prices to cover costs during difficult periods</li>\n  <li><strong>Return on investment (ROI):</strong> Price to achieve a target return on investment</li>\n  <li><strong>Quality leadership:</strong> Premium price to signal highest quality</li>\n  <li><strong>Social pricing:</strong> Keep prices affordable for social or public interest reasons</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Pricing Strategies</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Strategy</th><th>Description</th><th>When to Use</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Cost-plus pricing</td><td>Add a markup to total cost</td><td>When costs are the primary concern</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Penetration pricing</td><td>Low initial price to gain market share</td><td>New market entry; price-sensitive market</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Price skimming</td><td>High initial price; reduce gradually</td><td>Innovative product with no competitors; affluent target</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Competitive pricing</td><td>Price based on competitors' prices</td><td>Commodity markets; strong competition</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Psychological pricing</td><td>₦999 instead of ₦1,000 — seems cheaper</td><td>Retail consumer products</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Premium pricing</td><td>Deliberately high price to signal luxury/quality</td><td>Luxury brands; unique products</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Value-based pricing</td><td>Price based on perceived value to customer</td><td>Differentiated products; strong brands</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Factors Influencing/Determining Price</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Effect on Price</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Cost of production</td><td>Sets the floor — price must cover costs</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Competition</td><td>Competitive prices limit how high prices can be set</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Demand</td><td>Higher demand → higher price possible; lower demand → lower price</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Consumer perception</td><td>Perceived quality and value affects what consumers will pay</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Government regulations</td><td>Price controls, subsidies, VAT affect prices</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Company objectives</td><td>Profit vs market share vs survival objectives determine price level</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Economic conditions</td><td>Inflation, recession affect consumer purchasing power and cost of inputs</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Price is the ONLY revenue-generating P (all other Ps are costs). COST sets the FLOOR (minimum price). DEMAND and CONSUMER PERCEPTION set the CEILING (maximum price). Price SKIMMING = high first (Apple iPhone launch). PENETRATION = low first (new brand entering market). PSYCHOLOGICAL = ₦999 not ₦1,000.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Pricing objectives: profit, market share, survival, ROI, quality leadership. Strategies: cost-plus, penetration (low launch), price skimming (high launch), competitive, psychological (₦999), premium, value-based. Determinants: cost (floor), competition, demand, perception, government, company objectives, economic conditions.\n</div>\n  ",
