    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  This topic extends advertising knowledge to cover the <span class=\"learn-keyword\">advertising process</span>, ethical issues in advertising, and the regulatory framework governing advertising in Nigeria. Understanding these aspects ensures advertising is both effective and responsible.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. The Advertising Process</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Creating an effective advertising campaign involves several stages:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Setting advertising objectives:</strong> What do we want to achieve? (Awareness, attitude change, trial, loyalty)</li>\n  <li><strong>Setting advertising budget:</strong> How much to spend? (Percentage of sales, objective-and-task, competitive parity)</li>\n  <li><strong>Developing the advertising message:</strong> What to say and how to say it (creative strategy — USP, emotional appeal, rational appeal)</li>\n  <li><strong>Selecting the media:</strong> Which media channel best reaches the target audience at acceptable cost?</li>\n  <li><strong>Media scheduling:</strong> When and how often to advertise? (Continuous, pulsing, flighting schedules)</li>\n  <li><strong>Evaluating advertising effectiveness:</strong> Did the advertising achieve its objectives? (Pre-testing, post-testing)</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Advertising Agencies</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">An advertising agency is a specialist firm that plans, creates, and places advertising on behalf of clients. Nigerian advertising agencies include SO&ampU, DDB Lagos, Noah's Ark, and Insight Communications.</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Functions:</strong> Creative development, media planning and buying, market research, campaign management</li>\n  <li><strong>Benefit:</strong> Specialist expertise, creative talent, and media relationships that most companies don't have in-house</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Ethical Issues in Advertising</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>False/misleading advertising:</strong> Making untrue product claims</li>\n  <li><strong>Advertising to children:</strong> Targeting vulnerable young audiences with manipulative ads</li>\n  <li><strong>Stereotyping:</strong> Reinforcing harmful gender, ethnic, or racial stereotypes</li>\n  <li><strong>Promoting unhealthy products:</strong> Advertising alcohol, tobacco, junk food to vulnerable groups</li>\n  <li><strong>Invasion of privacy:</strong> Using personal data for targeted advertising without consent</li>\n  <li><strong>Subliminal advertising:</strong> Hidden messages influencing below conscious awareness</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Advertising Regulation in Nigeria</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Advertising Regulatory Council of Nigeria (ARCON):</strong> Regulates advertising industry; sets standards; ensures ethical advertising</li>\n  <li><strong>NAFDAC:</strong> Regulates advertising of food, drugs, and related products</li>\n  <li><strong>Nigerian Broadcasting Commission (NBC):</strong> Regulates content on radio and television</li>\n  <li><strong>Consumer Protection Council (CPC):</strong> Protects consumers from deceptive advertising</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> ARCON (Advertising Regulatory Council of Nigeria) is the PRIMARY advertising regulator in Nigeria. The six steps of the advertising process: Objectives → Budget → Message → Media → Schedule → Evaluate. The USP (Unique Selling Proposition) is the central promise that makes a product distinctively attractive.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Advertising process: set objectives → budget → develop message → select media → schedule → evaluate. Advertising agencies: specialist firms planning/creating/placing ads. Ethical issues: false claims, children, stereotyping, unhealthy products, privacy, subliminal. Nigerian regulators: ARCON (primary), NAFDAC (drugs/food), NBC (broadcast), CPC (consumer protection).\n</div>\n  ",
