    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  This topic extends pricing knowledge to cover additional pricing approaches, price adjustment strategies, and the impact of technology on pricing. Understanding advanced pricing enables businesses to optimise revenue in different market situations.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Price Adjustment Strategies</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Adjustment Strategy</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Discount pricing</td><td>Reduce price for bulk purchase, early payment, or cash</td><td>5% discount for paying within 7 days</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Segmented pricing</td><td>Different prices for different segments (same product, different prices)</td><td>Students/elderly discounts; peak/off-peak pricing</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Promotional pricing</td><td>Temporary price reduction to stimulate sales</td><td>Loss leaders, seasonal sales</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Geographic pricing</td><td>Different prices in different locations based on transport and market costs</td><td>Higher prices in remote areas</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>International pricing</td><td>Prices adjusted for different country markets</td><td>Same product priced differently in Lagos vs London</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. New Pricing Approaches (Technology-Driven)</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Dynamic pricing:</strong> Prices change in real-time based on demand (Uber surge pricing, airline fares)</li>\n  <li><strong>Freemium pricing:</strong> Basic version free; premium features paid (Spotify free vs premium)</li>\n  <li><strong>Subscription pricing:</strong> Recurring fee for ongoing access (Netflix monthly fee)</li>\n  <li><strong>Pay-what-you-want:</strong> Customers choose the price (some digital products, charity)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Price Wars and their Consequences</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>A price war occurs when competitors continuously undercut each other's prices</li>\n  <li>Result: reduced profitability for all competitors; potential exit of weaker players; may harm industry sustainability</li>\n  <li>Better alternative: compete on value (quality, service, brand) rather than price alone</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Transfer Pricing</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Transfer pricing is the price at which transactions occur between divisions of the same company (or between related international entities). It affects how profits are reported and taxed across different business units or countries.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> KEY price adjustment strategies: Discount (lower for volume/cash), Segmented (different segments pay different prices — cinema tickets), Promotional (temporary reduction), Geographic (location-based). DYNAMIC pricing = real-time price changes based on demand (Uber, airlines). FREEMIUM = free basic + paid premium (Spotify, Zoom).\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Price adjustments: discounts (volume/cash), segmented (different prices for different groups), promotional (temporary), geographic (location-based). New approaches: dynamic (real-time demand-based), freemium (free basic + paid premium), subscription (recurring fee). Price wars reduce profitability — compete on value, not just price.\n</div>\n  ",
