    "topic": "Promotion I (Third Term)",
    "topicCode": "SS1-MKT-19",
    "module": "Promotion",
    "term": "Third Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  This topic focuses specifically on <span class=\"learn-keyword\">sales promotion</span> — one of the key elements of the promotion mix. Sales promotions are short-term incentive tools designed to stimulate immediate trial or purchase of a product by consumers or trade partners.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Sales Promotion</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Sales promotion consists of short-term incentives to encourage the trial or purchase of a product or service. Unlike advertising (which builds long-term brand image), sales promotion is designed to generate immediate, short-term sales response.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Consumer Sales Promotion Tools</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Description</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Free samples</td><td>Free product given to encourage trial</td><td>Free sachet of shampoo in newspaper</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Coupons</td><td>Certificate offering discount on next purchase</td><td>₦200 off coupon for detergent</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cash refunds/rebates</td><td>Return of part of price after purchase proof</td><td>Send receipt; get ₦500 rebate</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Price packs (bonus packs)</td><td>Extra product for same price (10% more free)</td><td>'400g for price of 350g'</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Premiums (gifts)</td><td>Gift offered free or at low cost with purchase</td><td>Free cup with coffee purchase</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Contests/competitions</td><td>Chance to win prizes by completing entry criteria</td><td>Win a car — buy Pepsi, enter code</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Loyalty programmes</td><td>Points accumulated for purchases; redeemable for rewards</td><td>Shoprite rewards card</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Point-of-purchase (POP) displays</td><td>Special in-store displays promoting products</td><td>Brand-branded refrigerators in shops</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Trade (Retailer) Promotion Tools</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Trade discounts:</strong> Price reductions to retailers for stocking products</li>\n  <li><strong>Allowances:</strong> Payments to retailers for special display space or featuring in advertising</li>\n  <li><strong>Free goods:</strong> Extra merchandise given to retailers with certain order quantities</li>\n  <li><strong>Sales force contests:</strong> Incentives for salespeople who achieve targets</li>\n  <li><strong>Cooperative advertising:</strong> Manufacturer shares retailer's advertising costs for featuring the product</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Objectives of Sales Promotion</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Encourage trial of new products</li>\n  <li>Reward loyal customers</li>\n  <li>Increase purchase frequency or quantity</li>\n  <li>Counter competitor promotions</li>\n  <li>Boost slow-moving inventory</li>\n  <li>Build trade relationships</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Sales promotion = SHORT-TERM incentive for IMMEDIATE action. Key consumer tools: free samples (best for encouraging trial), coupons (discounts on next purchase), loyalty programmes (reward repeat buying), contests. Key trade tools: trade discounts, display allowances, free goods with orders. Unlike advertising, sales promotion does NOT build long-term brand equity.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Sales promotion = short-term incentives for immediate purchase. Consumer tools: samples, coupons, rebates, price packs, premiums, contests, loyalty programmes. Trade tools: trade discounts, allowances, free goods, sales contests. Objectives: trial, loyalty, frequency, counter competition, clear inventory. Different from advertising (long-term brand building).\n</div>\n  ",
