    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  This topic focuses on <span class=\"learn-keyword\">personal selling</span> and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">public relations</span> as promotion tools, and introduces <span class=\"learn-keyword\">digital marketing</span> as a modern promotional medium transforming how businesses communicate with customers.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Personal Selling</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Personal selling is the direct, face-to-face interaction between a salesperson and a prospective customer aimed at making a sale and building a customer relationship.</p>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><strong>The Personal Selling Process:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Prospecting:</strong> Identifying potential customers (leads)</li>\n  <li><strong>Pre-approach:</strong> Researching the prospect before the meeting</li>\n  <li><strong>Approach:</strong> Making the initial contact and first impression</li>\n  <li><strong>Presentation/demonstration:</strong> Presenting the product's benefits</li>\n  <li><strong>Handling objections:</strong> Addressing the customer's concerns</li>\n  <li><strong>Closing:</strong> Asking for the order</li>\n  <li><strong>Follow-up:</strong> After-sale relationship maintenance</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Public Relations (PR)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">PR involves building and maintaining good relationships with the company's various publics — media, customers, employees, investors, government, and community — to build positive image and goodwill.</p>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><strong>PR Tools:</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Press releases and press conferences</li>\n  <li>Sponsorships (sports, cultural, educational events)</li>\n  <li>Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) activities</li>\n  <li>Community relations programmes</li>\n  <li>Crisis management communications</li>\n  <li>Annual reports and company publications</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Digital Marketing as a Promotion Tool</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Social media marketing:</strong> Facebook, Instagram, Twitter/X, TikTok</li>\n  <li><strong>Content marketing:</strong> Creating valuable content that attracts and retains customers</li>\n  <li><strong>Search Engine Optimisation (SEO):</strong> Improving website visibility in search results</li>\n  <li><strong>Email marketing:</strong> Targeted email communications to subscribers</li>\n  <li><strong>Influencer marketing:</strong> Using social media personalities to promote products</li>\n  <li><strong>Pay-per-click (PPC) advertising:</strong> Ads paid for only when clicked</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Personal selling process: 7 steps (Prospect → Pre-approach → Approach → Present → Handle objections → Close → Follow-up). PR = EARNED/UNPAID media coverage (more credible than advertising). CSR activities generate PR goodwill. Digital marketing is the fastest-growing promotion medium.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Personal selling: 7-step process (prospecting to follow-up) — most effective for complex B2B products. PR: earned media through press releases, sponsorships, CSR, crisis management. Digital marketing: social media, content, SEO, email, influencers, PPC. All three are key promotion tools in the modern mix.\n</div>\n  ",
